        "notes": "Inspected broad south2007 elevation: long tiled nave, large pointed aisle windows with restrained geometric tracery, upper clerestory and stepped supports/flying arches. Distinct Romanesque transept gable/rose and three rounded lower windows above low open Renaissance porch. Higher choir with chapel ring and pronounced flying buttresses. Temporary west scaffolding, market stalls, people and nearby town excluded."
